\margin{\uline{NB}
(\inserted{si} \(\Sigma\) \unsure{est}
\unsure{séparé}, \unsure{donc} \(\Sigma\times\Sigma\) \unsure{séparé}
sur \(\Sigma\), et \(\Sigma^{\ast}(1)\mathrel{\overset{\underline b}{\rule[0.45ex]{2em}{0.4pt}}}\Sigma\)
\unsure{propre}, il est visible
que \(\Sigma^{\ast}(1)\mathrel{\rule[0.45ex]{2em}{0.4pt}}\Sigma\times\Sigma\) \unsure{est}
\unsure{propre} donc \unsure{un|une} \unsure{plongement}
\uline{\unsure{fermé|fermée}}.}
% si is above a long headless stroke preceding Sigma; its insertion/cancellation function is unresolved. Right-edge main-text fragments include se, en, p_2 and qui rende; at the lower edge the beginning of Cartésien is clipped. The marginal final word overlaps the main-text region.

\margin{cette condition de
transversalité est
peut être \unsure{conséquence}
des autres \unsure{?}}
% No hyphen is visibly inserted between peut and être. The terminal candidate question mark consists of a dot and a short hooked/oblique stroke. The upper edge clips a preceding marginal tail; the right edge clips main-line strokes, including à.

\deleted{\unsure{une immersion}}
\deleted{\(\unsure{\Sigma}\)}
% The lower Sigma-like character is multiply overdrawn by a broad zigzag and a left-curving stroke. A long near-horizontal cancellation passes through the upper words; three large enclosing/oblique revision strokes cross the box.
% At right, b) and the beginning of the raised candidate strict(e) are caught from adjoining lines.

\deleted{\inserted{\(\bigl(=\Sigma^{\unsure{\ast|t}}(1)_{\unsure{x}}\bigr)\)}
\unsure{est fini}}
% The inserted parenthesis is above the low baseline est fini. Its superscript is a short crossed/looping contour; the subscript is a thick small overwritten crossing beside a longer oblique stroke. A long curved brace-like stroke runs underneath the insertion and rises at right; large cancellation slashes pass through the formula and baseline. At upper edge is the clipped preceding word ending; at lower left is a clipped x from the preceding box.
